Hmm wait — hashJson with String.join("\u001F", categories) reintroduces separator collision inside. Better: pass the categories list directly as a JSON element. hashJson(Object... parts) serializes List.of(parts) — parts can include a List<String>. Jackson serializes nested list fine. So `hashJson("task_evidence_require", actor, incidentKey, taskKey, categories, expectedVersion)`. List.of() disallows null elements — categories is non-null list, fine. But List.of(parts) with parts containing a List is fine.

hashJson:
```java
    /**
     * 结构化请求身份摘要：将操作、操作者、资源及全部参数（含期望版本）序列化为 JSON 后取
     * SHA-256，避免分隔符拼接造成的碰撞。
     */
    private String hashJson(Object... identityParts) {
        try {
            MessageDigest digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
            byte[] out = digest.digest(objectMapper.writeValueAsString(Arrays.asList(identityParts))
                    .getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
            return HexFormat.of().formatHex(out);
        } catch (JsonProcessingException | NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("请求身份摘要计算失败", e);
        }
    }
